    },
    "findings": [],
    "reviewConclusions": {
      "plannerV7Preserved": "planVersion returns undefined when no per-version physical/restored-bounded candidates survive; outer [7,8] filter preserves eligible v7 and throws only if both fail. New test constructs v8 native fallback >20M while v7 remains valid and asserts schema7.",
      "manifestAccounting": "search-capacity-audit counts original manifest plus all actual baseline payloads and candidate manifest plus all actual candidate payloads. Candidate full budgets control strict admission; over-budget old baseline remains diagnostic only. search-v5-corpus-audit counts complete current and eachv5/v6/v7 comparison manifest once. Production generate.ts and verifySearchAssets remain unchanged full-manifest accounting delegates.",
      "legacyCompatibility": "Worker expands only physical-files route5/6/7 to5/6/7/8. Legacy shards route1-5 and logical-v4 import are unchanged. Emitted-worker matrix includes5/6/7/8 plus legacy1-5, corruption, lazy concurrency and late decode/import retry. v5-v7 writer fixture pins pre-v8 SHA256 outputs.",
      "actualV8Path": "Codec test explicitly asserts5channels and16 nonempty compact map rows. Worker channels fixture requires nonempty columns and5channels for8. Corpus files-v8 fixture separately selects version8 and requires nonempty5channel payload. Generate fixture permits7|8 intentionally because tiny inputs and unavailable-v8 cases may correctly select7.",
      "termState": "Encoder dictionary first appearance spans all maps; per-map reused previous resets and new terms do not alter it. Decoder traverses actual original shard.columnarMaps order including native arrays, bounds command-generated IDs and native-ID progression, and requires every dictionary entry introduced. Negative-rest maps remain original native arrays.",
